Feature: TC_27_STAFF - OpenShift View Application Screen E2E Regression Pack

  # --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  # Legacy  : "Regression Pack for Openshift View Application Cases" (BISSAGL-12967, AT-TC-01 to 08,
  #           tmslinks BISSAGL-12927 / 12928 / 12929 / 12930 / 13008 / 13009 / 13010 / 13011)
  # Rewritten 16-10-2026 in the StaffSteps vocabulary (the wording the MAPS features run with). One end-to-end
  # scenario on the OpenShift deployment; # SECTION markers show where each legacy scenario starts.
  #
  # Purpose:
  #   The application summary on OpenShift:
  #     - cancelling the Force Majeure dialog leaves the tick as it was (2025, 2024, 2023)
  #     - saving Force Majeure on and then off flips the tick and puts it back (2024, 2023)
  #     - a View details dialog opens and closes back to the summary
  #     - the Land Details info icon shows its tooltip
  #     - the Active Farmer screen opens
  #   The herd is left with the Force Majeure tick it started with.
  #
  # Legacy coverage notes carried forward:
  #   - Legacy clicked and saved without reading the tick; here it is read before and compared after every Cancel
  #     and Save.
  #   - AT-TC-05 only searched for the herd although its title is "View Active Farmer screen"; Section 5 opens it.
  #   - AT-TC-06 to 08 (Land Details, GAEC8 and Digitisation Task screens as agr11612) only logged in - those screens
  #     were never automated. Section 6 keeps the login; send the screen names / HTML and they can be added.
  #
  # Test data:
  #   Herds from the database ("Get Submitted Herds"), as in legacy: one herd for Sections 1-3 (legacy row 6), the
  #   next ones for Sections 4 and 5.
  #   Logins agr4442 (BISS Co-ordination 1) and agr11612 (as in legacy). Password: TD:Password from the TestData row of
  #   this test case, the same for both.
  #
  # Step definitions: stepdefinitions.BISS.STAFF.StaffSteps (Force Majeure and application dialogs)
  # Author: Aniket Pathare | aniket.pathare@government.ie
  # --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  @regression @staff @openshift @force-majeure @e2e
  Scenario: AT-STAFF-OS-VIEW-APP-E2E-01 - Staff uses Force Majeure, dialogs and tooltips on the OpenShift application summary

    # SECTION 1 : Cancel Force Majeure in three scheme years - AT-TC-01 (BISSAGL-12927)
    Given the staff user is logged in to the OpenShift BISS portal as "agr4442"
    When the staff user cancels a Force Majeure request for the same submitted herd across the following years
      | 2025 |
      | 2024 |
      | 2023 |
    Then the Force Majeure state should remain unchanged

    # SECTION 2 : Save Force Majeure on and off - AT-TC-02 (BISSAGL-12928)
    When the staff user applies and removes Force Majeure for the same submitted herd across the following years
      | year | applyNote | removeNote  |
      | 2024 | Test Save | Test UnSave |
      | 2023 | Test Save | Test UnSave |
    Then the Force Majeure state should remain unchanged

    # SECTION 3 : View details dialog - AT-TC-03 (BISSAGL-12929)
    When the staff user opens the application for the same submitted herd for scheme year "2024"
    And the staff user opens the application summary details dialog
    Then the dialog should close cleanly

    # SECTION 4 : Land Details info icon - AT-TC-04 (BISSAGL-12930)
    When the staff user opens the application for the next submitted herd for scheme year "2024"
    Then the "Determined area with compensation" info icon should expose its tooltip

    # SECTION 5 : Active Farmer screen - AT-TC-05 (BISSAGL-13008)
    When the staff user opens the application for the next submitted herd for scheme year "2024"
    And the staff user opens the "Active Farmer" screen
    Then the Active Farmer screen should be displayed

    # SECTION 6 : Second user login - AT-TC-06 to 08 (BISSAGL-13009 / 13010 / 13011)
    When the staff user signs out of the portal
    Given the staff user is logged in to the OpenShift BISS portal as "agr11612"
    Then the dashboard should remain available
